# Not written:
#   inside a VLAN: the rule is for zone vlan10-office, vlan20-servers, vlan30-ot-cell, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   office to servers web: the rule is for zone vlan10-office, vlan20-servers, vlan30-ot-cell, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   historian: the rule is for zone vlan10-office, vlan20-servers, vlan30-ot-cell, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   eng ws to plc: the rule is for zone vlan10-office, vlan20-servers, vlan30-ot-cell, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   block update site: host name object fqdn updates.example.com: a security rule names addresses
#   dns to servers: the rule is for zone vlan10-office, vlan20-servers, vlan30-ot-cell, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   ping servers: the rule is for zone vlan10-office, vlan20-servers, vlan30-ot-cell, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   office ipv6 out: the rule is for zone vlan10-office, vlan20-servers, vlan30-ot-cell, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   passive ftp: the rule is for zone vlan10-office, vlan20-servers, vlan30-ot-cell, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   bad ports: not converted: destination port '1024-5000,5004' cannot be read (one range, or a list of single ports); the rule is for zone vlan10-office, vlan20-servers, vlan30-ot-cell, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
#   Default rule: the rule is for zone vlan10-office, vlan20-servers, vlan30-ot-cell, and a security rule names no zone: give the networks behind it with --zone-network
